<script>let {email,preview=false,supportEmail='hello@gridubuntu.com'}=$props();</script>
<div class="page-heading"><div><div class="breadcrumb">YOUR ACCOUNT <span>/</span> HELP</div><h1>A little help, when you need it.</h1><p>Your account, access, and GridUbuntu support.</p></div></div>
<div class="system-grid"><section class="panel"><div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="overline">YOUR DETAILS</span><h2>Account & access</h2></div></div><div class="health-row"><span>Email address</span><strong>{email}</strong></div><div class="health-row"><span>Account access</span><strong>{preview?'Design preview':'Invited client'}</strong></div><div class="health-row"><span>Equipment permissions</span><strong>Read only</strong></div><p class="panel-note">Residence assignments are managed by GridUbuntu. Contact us if your residence details need correcting.</p>{#if !preview}<a class="portal-button secondary" href="/auth/set-password">Change password →</a>{:else}<span class="panel-note">Password management is available after secure sign-in.</span>{/if}</section><section class="panel"><div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="overline">WE’RE HERE TO HELP</span><h2>Contact GridUbuntu</h2></div></div><p class="support-text">Questions about your connection or an unexpected reading? Share your node reference and the reporting time with the GridUbuntu team.</p><a class="support-email" href={'mailto:'+supportEmail}>{supportEmail} ↗</a><a class="panel-link" href="/contact">Visit our contact page <span>→</span></a></section></div>
<section class="panel faq-panel"><span class="overline">COMMON QUESTIONS</span><h2>Understanding your portal</h2><details><summary>Why is a reading marked as delayed?</summary><p>The displayed measurement is more than 15 minutes old. The installation may not have uploaded recent data, or its connection may be interrupted. Check the reporting time and contact your operator if it persists.</p></details><details><summary>Why are some readings unavailable?</summary><p>Some installations do not have every sensor. A reading can also be missing while the provider connection is unavailable or the installation is being verified.</p></details><details><summary>Can I control my equipment here?</summary><p>No. This client release is for monitoring only. Device control remains with your operator.</p></details><details><summary>Where do the energy readings come from?</summary><p>Your assigned SunSynk installation reports to SunSynk’s VRM service. GridUbuntu retrieves the permitted data on the server and presents it in your portal. Reporting intervals depend on the installation.</p></details></section>
